<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan asset-backed shrs up on oil price worry.</title>
<headline>Taiwan asset-backed shrs up on oil price worry.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's construction and asset-backed shares rose at mid-morning on Monday on buying triggered by concerns over likely domestic oil price hikes by state Chinese Petroleum Corp, brokers said.</p>
<p>With 80 minutes left, constructions rose 0.16 percent while the overall index fell 0.02 percent.</p>
<p>BES Engineerning rose 40 cents or 1.53 percent to T$26.6 and Yuh Chen Construction rose by the daily seven percent limit to T$36.</p>
</text>
